{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYrjnSCntbHpakNjUa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI announced on October 30 that it will honor a common signal in robots.txt that lets website operators state their preference about whether their content is used for foundational generative AI training. The signal draws on work in the Internet Engineering Task Force's AI Preferences working group, and OpenAI made the announcement alongside other participants in that group.\n\nThe change addresses a specific maintenance burden for site operators. A publisher who wanted to set a training preference previously had to identify each provider's crawler and maintain a separate rule for every one. With a shared signal, an operator can state one preference that applies to every participating provider.\n\nThe announcement comes with several qualifications. OpenAI describes the effort as voluntary, so the signal reaches only providers that choose to honor it, and the article doesn't name which other providers have committed to doing so. OpenAI closes by encouraging other AI providers to adopt it, which suggests coverage is still incomplete. The signal is also not yet in effect at OpenAI. The company says it aims to implement it \"in the coming months\" and will share implementation details at that point.\n\nOpenAI's existing crawler controls in robots.txt will stay in place and continue to be respected. Operators who want provider-specific control can keep their current rules, and those who want a single statement about training gain a simpler option. The article doesn't explain how OpenAI will handle a site whose shared signal and crawler-specific rules point in different directions. That is one of the practical questions the promised implementation update will need to answer before operators can rely on the shared signal by itself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2012,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2012},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1c58e5a-4fa1-4fd6-b078-2371a23c2bb8","uuid":"50c2422b-c7a8-4a07-b775-89b52a86e0f5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:29:17.762Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYrjT6SDj6X5KymTaVz"}
